                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                        "entry_id": "c96492b4-fb8d-3eb5-a0a5-02c87c7fa3e5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In a stubbornly resolute manner; tenaciously holding one's course of action or opinion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6354bbb-cc00-4542-8896-392398e60fbc",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "Saint Augustine makes this difference betweene an heretike, and him that beleeves an heretike. The first begets or followes an errour pertinaciously."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4af52aec-48e2-4ea9-b632-b0b5d2072690",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "They shall therefore suffer punishment who reject this heavenly Light, and continue pertinaciously fix'd in those deadly principles which extinguish all knowledge of Virtue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5e3b20-0dd5-4f2d-bebf-dbbadfa9876a",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "No astronomical fallacy is more untenable, and none has been more pertinaciously adhered to, than that of the absolute illimitation of the Universe of Stars."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d92dc1d-6b5f-43df-b3c0-1da795a09035",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "I work with might and main against his Immigration Bill—as pertinaciously and as vindictively, indeed, as he works against our University."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d24444f-cece-4713-a45b-4eedc35218bd",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "If the great comedian [Charlie Chaplin] wishes to stay here in the country whose citizenship he has so pertinaciously retained, he will be less harassed and very welcome."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a7c14a-f1e2-4e5d-9066-88a60d3942ed",
                                "sense_id": "e04a408c-4742-3bed-9ee9-00a856888b54",
                                "text": "In Greater Poland (Wielkopolska) the middle class and part of the local gentry clung pertinaciously to Lutheranism."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
